# Localization

Partner Check uses **hand-maintained** l10n — no code generation.

## Locales (17)

`en`, `ar`, `he`, `cs`, `sk`, `zh`, `ja`, `nl`, `de`, `es`, `fr`, `hi`, `it`, `pl`, `hu`, `ru`, `pt`

RTL: `ar`, `he` — use `AppLocalizations.isRtl` / `directionality_utils.dart` for slide directions.

## Adding a string (all 3 steps required)

1. **`lib/l10n/app_en.arb`** — add key + `@key` description
2. **All 16 other `app_*.arb` files** — add translated value (English fallback acceptable if user hasn't provided translations)
3. **`lib/l10n/app_localizations.dart`**:
   - Simple: `String get myKey => _localizedValues[locale.languageCode]?['myKey'] ?? 'English fallback';`
   - Parameterized: `String myKey(String name) => (...).replaceAll('{name}', name);`
   - Add `'myKey': '...'` to **every** language block in `_localizedValues`

## Usage in UI

```dart
final l10n = AppLocalizations.of(context)!;
Text(l10n.contactLimitMessage)
Text(l10n.contactAlreadyInList(contactName))
```

Never hardcode user-visible strings in widgets or dialogs.
